Id: lin009i
Severity: INFO
Category: network
Check: check_network_config
Fix: Set net.ipv4.icmp_echo_ignore_all=1 in /etc/sysctl.d if the host should not answer pings.
References: sysctl.d(5); Linux kernel ip-sysctl documentation
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST SC-5, SC-7; ISO 8.20; CE Secure configuration

The kernel will answer (per configuration) to ICMP echo requests in any
interface. You might want to configure it to not answer to this requests
and thus make it more "invisible". Do it with:
 # sysctl -w net.ipv4.icmp_echo_ignore_all=1
Note, however, that this violates RFCs.
